  "id": "passive-rehearsal",
  "term": "passive rehearsal",
  "definition": "Passive rehearsal is a learning strategy in which a person repeats information while first taking it in, such as by rote memorization. In cognitive psychology, it is contrasted with active retrieval strategies that involve mentally working with or recalling the information.",
